<!--
    The Darwin stack probe and MachineOutliner fragments
    (`option chkstkdarwin on|off`, `option outlinedinline on|off`).

    Issue: an Apple function with a large frame calls `___chkstk_darwin`
    (size in x9; it preserves every register), but the default call model has
    the call clobber x0-x18, so a value kept in x8 across it printed as an
    undefined local beside a `__chkstk_darwin()` call. And clang's
    MachineOutliner splits functions into shared `OUTLINED_FUNCTION_<n>`
    fragments, which printed as opaque calls with nonsense arguments.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2. `p2_lift/kuna_chkstkdarwin.rs` deletes the probe
    CALL pre-SSA; `p2_lift/kuna_outlinedinline.rs` flags each fragment inline
    so flow splices it into the caller, and the inliner keeps a fragment's own
    RETURN when the caller tail-calls it.

    P0 assertions: `option chkstkdarwin on|off`, `option outlinedinline on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; every pass loads
    the plain arm64 `macho_arm64_outlined` fixture (see the fixtures README).

    Pass 1 (both options off) reproduces the BUGs: `_probe` calls
    `__chkstk_darwin` and returns an undefined `v1 + 1`, `_sum2` returns
    `_OUTLINED_FUNCTION_0() + 3`, `_bail` tail-calls `_OUTLINED_FUNCTION_1`.
    Pass 2 (both on, the shipped defaults) is the FIX: `_probe` returns
    `a0 + 1` (its `sub sp,sp,x9` with `x9 = x0 << 4` prints as
    `alloca(a0 << 4)` under `option alloca`, which reads x0 at 64 bits), `_sum2` returns `(a0 + a1) * 2 + 3`, `_bail` calls `exit(7)`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_arm64_outlined</com>
